# Build backend for THIRD-PARTY source distributions.
#
# Distinct from constraints/build.in, which covers this project's own
# hatchling backend. This file covers the backend pip needs to build other
# people's sdists.
#
# constraints/mutation.lock pins mutmut==2.5.1 and glob2==0.7. Neither
# publishes a wheel, and neither ships a pyproject.toml — they are legacy
# setup.py packages, so pip builds them with the implicit setuptools
# backend. Under plain `--require-hashes` pip verifies the sdist itself and
# then, because PEP 517 build isolation is still on, creates a temporary
# environment and downloads setuptools and wheel from the index unhashed,
# and executes them. Hash-verifying the sdist does not help if the thing
# that compiles it is unverified.
#
# Installing this lock first lets the mutation toolchain be installed with
# --no-build-isolation, so the sdist builds use these hash-verified tools
# and nothing is fetched outside a lock.
#
# Verified: `pip install --no-cache-dir --require-hashes -r mutation.lock`
# emits 12 build events and downloads setuptools; with this lock installed
# first and --no-build-isolation it downloads nothing.
setuptools
wheel
